 "supervisor_summary": "Research target (12m) $525.83 per current pre-split share. Meta has agreed not to issue Class C shares while the Delaware Class C suits are pending (trial set for April 19, 2027), which also holds back the planned ~$60B at-the-market sale; the model now books no ATM sales by the horizon and funds that gap with debt. The operating build is unchanged: ad revenue grows with the social ad market at a constant Meta share (WARC +14.6% in 2027, +10.6% in 2028; Omdia +12% in 2029), capex follows the post-print analyst estimates ($241B in 2027, $250B in 2028 and 2029), and D&A comes from the depreciation engine checked against construction-in-progress balances ($44B / $72B / $104B in 2027-29), so FoA margins fall from 38.5% to about 27% by 2029. Net interest comes from a net debt roll (net debt rising to ~$245B by end-2028). Legal items stay as before (New Mexico $25B penalty at 40%, $19.9B of accruals) and Reality Labs is valued once at -$53B.",
